    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04fe0df5_997217fa",
        "filename": "floss/pandora/server/host.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1968385
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-26T06:48:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m doing this intentionally. f-string provides the better readability but just a little bit slower. I\u0027m curious about if there any other reason that we don\u0027t want to use it?",
      "parentUuid": "34154308_4eb7e85e",
      "revId": "5dfbe3ca2ea299daacff20b2bd53c04606d1a497",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a5f6e0f_d52de18b",
        "filename": "floss/pandora/server/host.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1993150
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-27T06:34:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is defined in Google Python style guide. \nIt disallows the use of formatted string in logging function. Consider the case that the log level is set to exclude info and debug, if you write a formatted log message, the Python interpreter needs to compose the message before calling the function and it turns out useless. logging functions are designed the way to compose log message after the log level matches.",
      "parentUuid": "04fe0df5_997217fa",
      "revId": "5dfbe3ca2ea299daacff20b2bd53c04606d1a497",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "296c675b_86f133d0",
        "filename": "floss/pandora/server/host.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1599263
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-27T07:25:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for information. Some sophisticated logging systems handle the uninterpolated format string differently. Avoid using f-string reduce the risk of producing error in this case makes sense.",
      "parentUuid": "2a5f6e0f_d52de18b",
      "revId": "5dfbe3ca2ea299daacff20b2bd53c04606d1a497",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
