      "writtenOn": "2023-10-27T08:08:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there are only very few speed improved but with bad readability so I choose to go for this way. After do some search on the moma, it seems that there are also some security issues if we f-string in the logging function. So I agree to not use f-string in this cases.\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/google.com/g/ops-sword-eng/c/CfatuNZanl8/m/ljH5x20zAQAJ\n\nBut I feel we need to have better way to log the string. Because the string like\n\n```\nlogging.info(\u0027Hi this is an example var1 is %s var2 is %s so the function returns %s\u0027, var1, var2, var3)\n```\n\nCause high cognitive load. There are some discussions on the internet:\nhttps://discuss.python.org/t/safer-logging-methods-for-f-strings-and-new-style-formatting/13802, may be we can look for better way to do this in the future.",
      "parentUuid": "296c675b_86f133d0",
      "revId": "5dfbe3ca2ea299daacff20b2bd53c04606d1a497",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
